/span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove the photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-add-several-cars-at-once" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add several cars at once</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a VIN list</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-service-and-maintenance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Service and maintenance</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, under Service and maintenance.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.</li><li>Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.</li><li>You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.</li><li>It is read only: call or message us about a service.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-take-new-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take new listing photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car&#39;s page, press <b class="gd-ui">Add listing photos</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Take new photos</b> for a car already live).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot in the list. Press <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if one is not right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/610"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="610"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:70.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-price-limits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Price limits</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Price limits for every car</b>, at the bottom: type a <b class="gd-ui">Minimum a day</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Maximum a day</b> in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One car different? Open it: <b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b> has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-pickup-and-return-records-cars-you-referred-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> shows the car&#39;s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> shows their cars&#39; bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-studio-photos-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio photos (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.</li><li>Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.</li><li>We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'notices-profile-and-leaving', 'chapter', 'for-partner-rental-companies', 'Keep your details up to date, read our notices, and know how to take a car out of the program.

## Notifications

1. Account > Notifications lists our messages: trips that are complete, payments and listing news, with your email preferences beside them. We do not email you when a booking comes in or changes, because many bookings are cancelled: the bookings coming up are always under Cars > Bookings. We email you when a trip is complete and the car is back (the dates, the days, the distance driven when it was recorded and your share of the trip; while your share is not shown to you yet, the email says it will show on your next statement), and once a week.
2. Press **Mark as read** on one, or **Mark all as read**.

![](/guides/img/owner-14-notifications-desktop-8e58b95e.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 692; address: carmacars.ca/owner/notifications; pins: 2 20.1 22.7")

## Your profile

1. Update your phone and address, then press Save. To change the email you sign in with, press **Change my email** under Sign-in: type the new address, open the link we send to it (the old address is told too), and your email changes everywhere.
2. On your agreements shows your legal name and how you are enrolled. A change to these means new agreements, so call or message us.

![](/guides/img/owner-15-profile-desktop-874dd23d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 872; address: carmacars.ca/owner/profile; pins: 1 12.2 84.7, 2 73.4 21.2")

## Texts or email

On **Account** > **Profile**, under **Messages**, choose **Email**, **Text** or **Both**: completed trips, payouts, invoices and documents to sign by a short text with a link. Texts need a phone you verified with a code. Statements, invoices and signed documents are always emailed too. Reply STOP to any text to stop them.

## Take a car out of the program

You give 30 days'' notice for that car only. Your other cars stay in.

1. Open Cars and the car. Read Leaving: when the notice ends and what happens to your last fees.
2. Press **Give notice**. Add a Reason (optional).
3. Press **Give exit notice**. The car''s page then shows its exit date.

## Phone alerts

Get an alert on your phone or computer when one of your cars is booked, when a booking changes, for payouts and payments, incidents and documents to sign.

1. Open **Account** > **Profile**. Under **Phone alerts**, press **Turn on alerts** and allow notifications when your browser asks.
2. Under **What to alert me about**, choose the topics. Your choice applies to all your devices.
3. **Send a test alert** shows one. **Turn off on this device** stops them there; **Remove** takes another device off.

Once your application is approved, your portal asks once whether to turn alerts on: press **Turn on**, or **Not now** (it is not asked again until a later approval). On a phone, once the CarmaCars app is in the stores, the invitation offers **Download the CarmaCars app** instead.

On iPhone and iPad, add CarmaCars to your Home Screen first (Safari, **Share**, **Add to Home Screen**), then open it from there and turn alerts on. Alerts that are not urgent wait until 8 am.

## Delete my account

**Profile**, **Delete my account**, then **Yes, delete my account**. We settle your cars, payouts and invoices first (a car under your agreement leaves the program with 30 days'' notice), then delete your account and email you. **Keep my account** withdraws the request. Agreements, statements and tax records are kept as the law requires.

## Your name and password (release 34)
Open Profile. **Save my display name** changes how you are greeted, at once. Your legal name is the one on your signed agreements, so it is not edited freely: press **Request a name change**, write the full name and why, and an Admin approves it. Until then the name on file stays. To change your email, use Change my email under Sign-in; to add or change your phone, use the phone box under Sign-in (we text a code). **Change my password** sends you to the password page.

## Your week, every Monday (release 41)

Every Monday morning (about 9:00 Toronto time) you get one email, only if there was something to tell. For each car: the trips completed last week with their dates and your share (a trip whose amount is not shown to you yet says it is on your statement), your confirmed bookings in the next 14 days (dates only), and your earnings so far this month, which are provisional until your statement. Only bookings that count toward your revenue are listed. Nothing to set up; it is on by default.
